# JAK1 Inhibitor pIC50 Predictor

A hybrid Graph Attention Network (GAT) and Streamlit web application for predicting the inhibitory potency (pIC50) of small molecules against Janus Kinase 1 (JAK1).

## Overview
The model combines molecular graph representations (3-layer GATConv) with 1,301 selected 2D RDKit descriptors and Morgan fingerprints. It achieved an R2 of 0.8701 on the held-out test set and was validated using 30-iteration X-Scrambling (`validation_x_scrambling.py`).

## Dataset
Due to GitHub file size limits, the full curated dataset (`7000.xlsx`) is hosted externally:
[Download 7000.xlsx via Google Drive](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15QUSk91LHd5MgHH6BIlFYuscHMTEsRxu/edit?gid=451988406#gid=451988406)

Note: The web app does not require `7000.xlsx` to run because the pre-fitted scaler is saved in `my_scaler.pkl`.

## Files
- `app.py`: Streamlit web interface and inference engine.
- `validation_x_scrambling.py`: X-Scrambling and feature importance validation script.
- `jak1_gat_7000_best.pth`: Trained PyTorch model weights.
- `my_scaler.pkl`: Pre-fitted StandardScaler.
- `best.vv.csv`: Selected 1,301 features.
- `x_scrambling_7000_1301_report.csv`: Validation report.
- `feature_audit_report_7000.csv` & `clean_features_7000.csv`: Feature auditing metadata.
- `requirements.txt`: Python dependencies.

## Usage
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/yousifh852004-dot/JAK1-pIC50-Predictor.git](https://github.com/yousifh852004-dot/JAK1-pIC50-Predictor.git)
cd JAK1-pIC50-Predictor
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```
